# {{project_name}}

The Lattice spec is the contract for this project. Code is correct when `./check.sh` passes.

## Commands
- `./check.sh` : run all Lattice checks (run after every group of edits; may take a while, a full run can call an LLM and cost money, prefer targeted runs when available).
- `check_run` tool: same checks through MCP, returns structured findings.

## Protected files
Do not edit: `{{requirements_path}}`, `{{spec_path}}`, `{{trace_path}}`. A PreToolUse hook denies these edits (including via shell). They are protected because the spec is what the code is judged against; changing it to pass a check defeats the check.

## Working with the spec
- Read: `model_get`, `rule_get`, `code_links`, `graph_get`.
- Ask: `spec_ask` (answers cite rule ids).
- Lint: `spec_lint`.
- Change the spec: `change_propose`, then ask the user to review and accept it in Lattice Studio. You cannot accept changes.

## Rules of thumb
- Fix findings in code, quoting the rule id. Never silence or weaken a check.
- If a rule looks wrong, propose a change; do not work around it.
- Keep edits small and rerun `./check.sh` until it passes.
